msgid "An optional [stream profile](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/stream_profile.h) binds immutable capacity assumptions to one selected continuous UART or ADC face. The [resolver](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/stream_profiles.py) generates this constant only when the assembly authors a profile. Factory lookup returns that existing profile; it neither creates a pool nor starts acquisition. Unprofiled entry points retain their own contracts and do not implicitly enforce this profile."
msgstr "An optional [stream profile](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/stream_profile.h) binds immutable capacity assumptions to one selected continuous UART or ADC face. The [resolver](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/stream_profiles.py) generates this constant only when the assembly authors a profile. Factory lookup returns that existing profile; it neither creates a pool nor starts acquisition. Unprofiled entry points retain their own contracts and do not implicitly enforce this profile."

msgid "The current F407/F470 double-buffer modes require two hardware targets, one replacement and enough additional blocks for the declared FIFO-frontier release delay. The calculation rounds retained blocks up and checks integer overflow, the 32-bit address extent and the 16-bit DMA counter. Target-replacement latency must be strictly shorter than a block's declared fill time. UART units are bytes; ADC units are complete scans containing one `uint16_t` per selected channel. ADC resolution bits do not change this storage width."
msgstr "The current F407/F470 double-buffer modes require two hardware targets, one replacement and enough additional blocks for the declared FIFO-frontier release delay. The calculation rounds retained blocks up and checks integer overflow, the 32-bit address extent and the 16-bit DMA counter. Target-replacement latency must be strictly shorter than a block's declared fill time. UART units are bytes; ADC units are complete scans containing one `uint16_t` per selected channel. ADC resolution bits do not change this storage width."

msgid "Cold profile admission checks the caller's actual block count, equal capacities, existing loans, state and payload/control disjointness before invoking the original provider. Pool users must already be joined. Alias checking is bounded by the configured pool and is quadratic; it adds no checks to the IRQ or steady data path. The application still owns pool storage, consumer release order and execution progress. Rate, release delay and IRQ latency are authored assumptions, with `physical_qualified = false`. Exhaustion stops and reports a gap. It does not create UART backpressure, lossless transport or preservation of ADC samples that would have occurred while the trigger was stopped."
msgstr "Cold profile admission checks the caller's actual block count, equal capacities, existing loans, state and payload/control disjointness before invoking the original provider. Pool users must already be joined. Alias checking is bounded by the configured pool and is quadratic; it adds no checks to the IRQ or steady data path. The application still owns pool storage, consumer release order and execution progress. Rate, release delay and IRQ latency are authored assumptions, with `physical_qualified = false`. Exhaustion stops and reports a gap. It does not create UART backpressure, lossless transport or preservation of ADC samples that would have occurred while the trigger was stopped."

