msgid "The existing `factory.capabilities` switch controls generated read-only trait objects. [Selected I/O traits](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/io_traits.py) describe a reviewed provider and mode, including formats, limits, abort scope, continuity, timestamp origin and DMA policy. Turning the switch off emits no new trait objects. It does not change the two-pointer base face or add mutable device state."
msgstr "The existing `factory.capabilities` switch controls generated read-only trait objects. [Selected I/O traits](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/io_traits.py) describe a reviewed provider and mode, including formats, limits, abort scope, continuity, timestamp origin and DMA policy. Turning the switch off emits no new trait objects. It does not change the two-pointer base face or add mutable device state."

msgid "A continuity value such as `double_buffer` or `rearm_gap` describes a mechanism, not demonstrated throughput. A Cache line requirement describes the selected provider policy, not proof that a particular clock profile enabled Cache. CAN mailbox counts are provider-specific facts. Traits grant neither Board wiring authorization nor physical qualification and cannot override admission checks."
msgstr "A continuity value such as `double_buffer` or `rearm_gap` describes a mechanism, not demonstrated throughput. A Cache line requirement describes the selected provider policy, not proof that a particular clock profile enabled Cache. CAN mailbox counts are provider-specific facts. Traits grant neither Board wiring authorization nor physical qualification and cannot override admission checks."

msgid "Controller and endpoint records describe their own interfaces. Do not apply a parent controller's byte-SPI or ordinary-I2C limits to an enhanced endpoint. A per-request word-width marker does not mean unlimited length. Check the selected face, count units and provider limit before allocating caller storage."
msgstr "Controller and endpoint records describe their own interfaces. Do not apply a parent controller's byte-SPI or ordinary-I2C limits to an enhanced endpoint. A per-request word-width marker does not mean unlimited length. Check the selected face, count units and provider limit before allocating caller storage."

