msgid "F407 and F470 RX-only DMA modes now use a compact receive owner with ordinary IRQ TX. Only a duplex DMA mode embeds the separate TX-DMA extension. Both reuse the same receive loan algorithm and shared read-only public operations layout; there is no stored optional implementation pointer or runtime TX-provider selection. RX-only operation does not acquire or withdraw the unrelated TX-DMA lane. Duplex vectors decode their real outer owner and its separate components. The receive pool excludes the complete duplex object, including its extension."
msgstr "F407 and F470 RX-only DMA modes now use a compact receive owner with ordinary IRQ TX. Only a duplex DMA mode embeds the separate TX-DMA extension. Both reuse the same receive loan algorithm and shared read-only public operations layout; there is no stored optional implementation pointer or runtime TX-provider selection. RX-only operation does not acquire or withdraw the unrelated TX-DMA lane. Duplex vectors decode their real outer owner and its separate components. The receive pool excludes the complete duplex object, including its extension."

msgid "RX and TX admission exclude both the TX payload and the complete TX request descriptor from every future RX target, in both admission orders. Stopping first closes admission and drains RX producer and consumer loans, then drains selected TX memory and wire activity, and finally withdraws the UART and RX vector. Failed drain retains the corresponding storage and responsibility. Actual linked ELF comparisons determine Flash and RAM savings; host `sizeof` expectations alone do not establish MCU costs or an unchanged instruction path."
msgstr "RX and TX admission exclude both the TX payload and the complete TX request descriptor from every future RX target, in both admission orders. Stopping first closes admission and drains RX producer and consumer loans, then drains selected TX memory and wire activity, and finally withdraws the UART and RX vector. Failed drain retains the corresponding storage and responsibility. Actual linked ELF comparisons determine Flash and RAM savings; host `sizeof` expectations alone do not establish MCU costs or an unchanged instruction path."

#: docs/design/io-evolution.md:176
msgid ""
"The separate H743 `dma-duplex-continuous` selection combines continuous RX "
"with finite TX DMA on one USART3 owner. Its exact V/HSI64/baremetal "
"reference uses AXI SRAM with Cache off or on; requests and the complete RX "
"pool remain disjoint and borrowed through their respective drain. The "
"existing `rx-dma-continuous` selection retains IRQ TX. See the [H743 "
"provider contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32/stm32h743/README.md#selected-continuous-rx-"
"and-finite-tx-dma-duplex) for the three-vector, cold-restart and retained-"
"taint boundaries. Neither selection expands to RTOS, PLL384 or D2 RAM."
msgstr ""
"The separate H743 `dma-duplex-continuous` selection combines continuous RX "
"with finite TX DMA on one USART3 owner. Its exact V/HSI64/baremetal "
"reference uses AXI SRAM with Cache off or on; requests and the complete RX "
"pool remain disjoint and borrowed through their respective drain. The "
"existing `rx-dma-continuous` selection retains IRQ TX. See the [H743 "
"provider contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32/stm32h743/README.md#selected-continuous-rx-"
"and-finite-tx-dma-duplex) for the three-vector, cold-restart and retained-"
"taint boundaries. Neither selection expands to RTOS, PLL384 or D2 RAM."

msgid "The synchronous whole-CS interface validates every segment and data span before hardware use. A null TX pointer means repeated dummy words, a null RX pointer means discard, and both may be null for clock-only phases. All segments share one asserted CS interval. Polling return releases the synchronous borrow only after CS is released and either wire drain or provider reset is proven; timeout cannot preempt an in-flight word. An error never replays earlier command phases. The asynchronous segmented interface has a separate admission, descriptor and cancellation contract."
msgstr "The synchronous whole-CS interface validates every segment and data span before hardware use. A null TX pointer means repeated dummy words, a null RX pointer means discard, and both may be null for clock-only phases. All segments share one asserted CS interval. Polling return releases the synchronous borrow only after CS is released and either wire drain or provider reset is proven; timeout cannot preempt an in-flight word. An error never replays earlier command phases. The asynchronous segmented interface has a separate admission, descriptor and cancellation contract."

msgid "The STM32F407/GD32F470 segmented DMA mechanism is a service-driven finite chain. Hardware DMA moves one segment, then the owner proves its drain before service arms the next. CS stays asserted across segments, but SCK gaps are permitted; this is not hardware linked-list DMA or a gapless transfer guarantee. The request, all descriptors, all spans and explicit fixed dummy/discard cells stay borrowed until acquire-observed SETTLED. Intermediate completion, cancel and timeout do not release them. Caller-driven service remains necessary; wake attachment and recovery capabilities cannot be inferred from the base SPI port."
msgstr "The STM32F407/GD32F470 segmented DMA mechanism is a service-driven finite chain. Hardware DMA moves one segment, then the owner proves its drain before service arms the next. CS stays asserted across segments, but SCK gaps are permitted; this is not hardware linked-list DMA or a gapless transfer guarantee. The request, all descriptors, all spans and explicit fixed dummy/discard cells stay borrowed until acquire-observed SETTLED. Intermediate completion, cancel and timeout do not release them. Caller-driven service remains necessary; wake attachment and recovery capabilities cannot be inferred from the base SPI port."

msgid "The optional [segmented SPI owner](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/bus_owner/include/nexus/components/spi_dma_owner.h) adapts this enhanced face to the existing bounded BusOwner queue. Caller-supplied slots and epochs remain the queue authority; no worker, payload copy or second controller owner is added. One uniquely scheduled executor services the inner request. Only after acquire-observed inner SETTLED does it detach private descriptor references and allow outer settlement. Queue time counts toward the outer deadline. Failed drain retains inner and outer borrows; late cancellation cannot replace an earlier terminal result."
msgstr "The optional [segmented SPI owner](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/bus_owner/include/nexus/components/spi_dma_owner.h) adapts this enhanced face to the existing bounded BusOwner queue. Caller-supplied slots and epochs remain the queue authority; no worker, payload copy or second controller owner is added. One uniquely scheduled executor services the inner request. Only after acquire-observed inner SETTLED does it detach private descriptor references and allow outer settlement. Queue time counts toward the outer deadline. Failed drain retains inner and outer borrows; late cancellation cannot replace an earlier terminal result."

msgid "An owner binding must prove that the endpoint's actual provider controller matches the selected enhanced controller. Matching a common sequence table and logical parent pointer alone is insufficient. The Native word model supplies an independent backend and checks its actual model-controller identity; it models 8/16-bit words, fixed cells, selected CS, faults and retained drain rather than forwarding to a byte-SPI implementation. A model's controller identity is a software identity, not observed silicon. Family hooks, generated owner bindings, publisher handoff and each target's execution evidence remain separate checks. Join publishers and observers before reclaiming their storage; an empty queue or a stopped transfer alone is not publisher join."
msgstr "An owner binding must prove that the endpoint's actual provider controller matches the selected enhanced controller. Matching a common sequence table and logical parent pointer alone is insufficient. The Native word model supplies an independent backend and checks its actual model-controller identity; it models 8/16-bit words, fixed cells, selected CS, faults and retained drain rather than forwarding to a byte-SPI implementation. A model's controller identity is a software identity, not observed silicon. Family hooks, generated owner bindings, publisher handoff and each target's execution evidence remain separate checks. Join publishers and observers before reclaiming their storage; an empty queue or a stopped transfer alone is not publisher join."

msgid "I2C hardware reload advances a long message without inserting another address phase. STOP and successful bus-idle observation precede successful return. On failure, the returned byte count records provider progress, including writes handed to TXDR before their wire ACK is known. The count does not authorize replay. Cancellation or failure does not justify replaying an acknowledged prefix or silently performing bus recovery. The enhanced face and base I2C interface share one executor. Timing inputs must include their reviewed clock and electrical bounds; a calculation is not a measurement of rise time or clock stretching. After physical STOP and bus idle are proved, refused STOP-flag or CR2 cleanup reports IO and preserves the actual progress count. The controller retains fault responsibility and rejects new admission until explicit recovery; already-drained caller storage may return."
msgstr "I2C hardware reload advances a long message without inserting another address phase. STOP and successful bus-idle observation precede successful return. On failure, the returned byte count records provider progress, including writes handed to TXDR before their wire ACK is known. The count does not authorize replay. Cancellation or failure does not justify replaying an acknowledged prefix or silently performing bus recovery. The enhanced face and base I2C interface share one executor. Timing inputs must include their reviewed clock and electrical bounds; a calculation is not a measurement of rise time or clock stretching. After physical STOP and bus idle are proved, refused STOP-flag or CR2 cleanup reports IO and preserves the actual progress count. The controller retains fault responsibility and rejects new admission until explicit recovery; already-drained caller storage may return."

msgid "ADC decoding reads only consumer-owned or acquired, producer-detached storage. It handles one-to-four-byte integer samples without allocating, retaining a pointer or performing calibrated voltage conversion. The consumer must first join producer/DMA access. Declared regular/injected groups and trigger identities describe an already supported mode; they do not start conversion or turn a software observation into a sample-aperture timestamp."
msgstr "ADC decoding reads only consumer-owned or acquired, producer-detached storage. It handles one-to-four-byte integer samples without allocating, retaining a pointer or performing calibrated voltage conversion. The consumer must first join producer/DMA access. Declared regular/injected groups and trigger identities describe an already supported mode; they do not start conversion or turn a software observation into a sample-aperture timestamp."

msgid "The G474 `shared-fixed-pwm` selection gives two ordinary PWM factory faces one physical TIM3 owner: CH1/PA6 and CH2/PA7 AF2, with a common fixed 170 MHz kernel, tick and period. The two existing declarations derive one cold construction, two readonly channel references, compatible base claims and exclusive lane/pad claims. There is no authored share flag, runtime registry, timer IRQ or DMA. Each set changes only its own CCR preload. A channel joining a running peer adopts the current phase without UG or counter restart; independent calls do not provide coherent group start or a full first pulse. Channel stop preserves the peer and establishes its own declared inactive GPIO level; only the last lane stops CEN. The lifecycle caller quiesces both channel users before final Platform stop. Physical close precedes outer pin/clock release, retaining cleanup responsibility if reset, inactive-level or restoration proof fails. The [canonical software reference](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/g474-pwm-shared.toml) requires the complete pair and excludes other whole-TIM3 or PA6/PA7 owners. Its Board choices do not establish PCB wiring, electrical safety or HIL."
msgstr "The G474 `shared-fixed-pwm` selection gives two ordinary PWM factory faces one physical TIM3 owner: CH1/PA6 and CH2/PA7 AF2, with a common fixed 170 MHz kernel, tick and period. The two existing declarations derive one cold construction, two readonly channel references, compatible base claims and exclusive lane/pad claims. There is no authored share flag, runtime registry, timer IRQ or DMA. Each set changes only its own CCR preload. A channel joining a running peer adopts the current phase without UG or counter restart; independent calls do not provide coherent group start or a full first pulse. Channel stop preserves the peer and establishes its own declared inactive GPIO level; only the last lane stops CEN. The lifecycle caller quiesces both channel users before final Platform stop. Physical close precedes outer pin/clock release, retaining cleanup responsibility if reset, inactive-level or restoration proof fails. The [canonical software reference](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/g474-pwm-shared.toml) requires the complete pair and excludes other whole-TIM3 or PA6/PA7 owners. Its Board choices do not establish PCB wiring, electrical safety or HIL."

msgid "PWM group commit stages one coherent shadow batch; `SUCCESS` does not prove the timer already applied it. A partial hardware-write failure must withdraw output and retain fault responsibility. Clearing a break does not enable output. The ordinary G474 PWM-group provider does not supply PCB pin selection, analog threshold measurements or a power stage, and does not itself create a synchronized ADC session. A selected software reference now generates exclusive TIM1/COMP1 construction, fixed PA8/PA9/PA10 PWM pads and PA1/PA4 comparator pads. Its cold lifecycle owns the selected clock/reset, safe levels, comparator setup and settling, shared break vector and reverse cleanup. Partial cleanup failure retains responsibility. The separate [finite coupled PWM/ADC owner](pwm-adc.md) now binds one fixed TIM1/ADC1/COMP1/DMA window without independently startable PWM-group or ADC subfaces. Neither selection establishes a fitted PCB route or analog accuracy."
msgstr "PWM group commit stages one coherent shadow batch; `SUCCESS` does not prove the timer already applied it. A partial hardware-write failure must withdraw output and retain fault responsibility. Clearing a break does not enable output. The ordinary G474 PWM-group provider does not supply PCB pin selection, analog threshold measurements or a power stage, and does not itself create a synchronized ADC session. A selected software reference now generates exclusive TIM1/COMP1 construction, fixed PA8/PA9/PA10 PWM pads and PA1/PA4 comparator pads. Its cold lifecycle owns the selected clock/reset, safe levels, comparator setup and settling, shared break vector and reverse cleanup. Partial cleanup failure retains responsibility. The separate [finite coupled PWM/ADC owner](pwm-adc.md) now binds one fixed TIM1/ADC1/COMP1/DMA window without independently startable PWM-group or ADC subfaces. Neither selection establishes a fitted PCB route or analog accuracy."

msgid "Separate concrete G474 providers implement TIM5 CH1 capture on PA0 and TIM3 two-input quadrature counting on PA6/PA7. Capture publishes raw 32-bit counter facts and explicit overcapture/loss under its bounded ring contract. Encoder reports a raw 16-bit count; it does not extend wrap, supply an index input or estimate speed. Separate [capture](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tests/contracts/g474_control_assembly/timer-capture.toml) and [encoder](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tests/contracts/g474_control_assembly/encoder.toml) software references now generate their own static faces, typed getters and cold pin/clock/vector lifecycle with whole-timer ownership and source/vector drain. Startup starts neither a capture session nor encoder counting. The application supplies the capture ring and explicitly starts and stops each session. Failed source/vector or storage drain retains cleanup responsibility. These exact selections do not inherit PWM-group capabilities, synchronize ADC apertures or establish external wiring. Product control and recovery policies remain external."
msgstr "Separate concrete G474 providers implement TIM5 CH1 capture on PA0 and TIM3 two-input quadrature counting on PA6/PA7. Capture publishes raw 32-bit counter facts and explicit overcapture/loss under its bounded ring contract. Encoder reports a raw 16-bit count; it does not extend wrap, supply an index input or estimate speed. Separate [capture](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tests/contracts/g474_control_assembly/timer-capture.toml) and [encoder](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tests/contracts/g474_control_assembly/encoder.toml) software references now generate their own static faces, typed getters and cold pin/clock/vector lifecycle with whole-timer ownership and source/vector drain. Startup starts neither a capture session nor encoder counting. The application supplies the capture ring and explicitly starts and stops each session. Failed source/vector or storage drain retains cleanup responsibility. These exact selections do not inherit PWM-group capabilities, synchronize ADC apertures or establish external wiring. Product control and recovery policies remain external."

msgid "Preserve a single owner for H743 Flash timing"
msgstr "Preserve a single owner for H743 Flash timing"

msgid "The selected fixed-HSI32/64 Flash path checks actual clock, requested and observed voltage scale, Cache state and Flash programming-delay fields before a program or erase pulse. Read latency alone does not satisfy the programming contract. An optional cold timing owner changes the reviewed Flash field only with both banks idle, verifies readback and retains its saved state until reverse cleanup has safely restored it. The generated Flash assembly selects this owner; a build without Flash does not acquire it. Product erase regions and recovery policy remain outside this repository."
msgstr "The selected fixed-HSI32/64 Flash path checks actual clock, requested and observed voltage scale, Cache state and Flash programming-delay fields before a program or erase pulse. Read latency alone does not satisfy the programming contract. An optional cold timing owner changes the reviewed Flash field only with both banks idle, verifies readback and retains its saved state until reverse cleanup has safely restored it. The generated Flash assembly selects this owner; a build without Flash does not acquire it. Product erase regions and recovery policy remain outside this repository."

msgid "This is a bounded programming-timing correction for the selected existing clock profiles. It does not enable a new high-speed clock, change option bytes, qualify all silicon revisions or establish physical Flash endurance. The separate selected [V-only HSI/PLL384 reference](h743-high-clock.md) now implements distinct CPU/bus/kernel clock domains and a cold clock/voltage/Flash lifecycle. Its joint owner replaces the fixed-HSI Flash timing owner for that high profile; support does not extend to unreviewed cuts, Cache-on execution or physical qualification."
msgstr "This is a bounded programming-timing correction for the selected existing clock profiles. It does not enable a new high-speed clock, change option bytes, qualify all silicon revisions or establish physical Flash endurance. The separate selected [V-only HSI/PLL384 reference](h743-high-clock.md) now implements distinct CPU/bus/kernel clock domains and a cold clock/voltage/Flash lifecycle. Its joint owner replaces the fixed-HSI Flash timing owner for that high profile; support does not extend to unreviewed cuts, Cache-on execution or physical qualification."

msgid "The selected V/cache-off Flash implementation now requires the [private RAM maintenance boundary](h743-flash-ram.md): cold copy/readiness, one selected workspace, a CPU-only stack bridge, RAM-owned VTOR and a temporary MPU guard. Deadline expiry after trigger only latches the result; actual both-bank drain, LOCK and protection/vector restoration precede any return. Production-ELF closure and complete software exits remain open, so IO-24 stays `in_progress`."
msgstr "The selected V/cache-off Flash implementation now requires the [private RAM maintenance boundary](h743-flash-ram.md): cold copy/readiness, one selected workspace, a CPU-only stack bridge, RAM-owned VTOR and a temporary MPU guard. Deadline expiry after trigger only latches the result; actual both-bank drain, LOCK and protection/vector restoration precede any return. Production-ELF closure and complete software exits remain open, so IO-24 stays `in_progress`."

msgid "Observe time without inventing timing guarantees"
msgstr "Observe time without inventing timing guarantees"

msgid "[Timestamp facts](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/observation.h) distinguish hardware events, IRQ observations, service observations and acquire observations. A caller supplies extended ticks, a domain, an epoch, an exact stated tick rate and explicit uncertainty knowledge. The domain owner extends counter wrap and changes epoch after discontinuity, reset or rate change."
msgstr "[Timestamp facts](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/observation.h) distinguish hardware events, IRQ observations, service observations and acquire observations. A caller supplies extended ticks, a domain, an epoch, an exact stated tick rate and explicit uncertainty knowledge. The domain owner extends counter wrap and changes epoch after discontinuity, reset or rate change."

msgid "Elapsed-time comparison requires matching domain, epoch and rate, ordered ticks and a representable uncertainty bound. It does not synchronize clocks, convert time domains, access a hardware clock or prove that two facts refer to causally paired events. Unknown uncertainty is different from a known zero bound."
msgstr "Elapsed-time comparison requires matching domain, epoch and rate, ordered ticks and a representable uncertainty bound. It does not synchronize clocks, convert time domains, access a hardware clock or prove that two facts refer to causally paired events. Unknown uncertainty is different from a known zero bound."

msgid "The optional timestamp budget evaluator consumes these same facts in O(1) work. It reports `WITHIN` only when the complete error interval fits the inclusive maximum, `EXCEEDED` only when its lower bound exceeds that maximum, and `UNKNOWN` otherwise. A successful comparison does not by itself mean within budget. The public timestamp contract owns the exact units and errors."
msgstr "The optional timestamp budget evaluator consumes these same facts in O(1) work. It reports `WITHIN` only when the complete error interval fits the inclusive maximum, `EXCEEDED` only when its lower bound exceeds that maximum, and `UNKNOWN` otherwise. A successful comparison does not by itself mean within budget. The public timestamp contract owns the exact units and errors."

msgid "Checked UART/SPI/I2C service reports an invalid face or an absent service method. `SUCCESS` establishes one dispatch only. It does not establish progress, health, SETTLED, wire completion or permission to reclaim storage. The ordinary service context, serialization and lifetime rules still apply, with no hidden worker."
msgstr "Checked UART/SPI/I2C service reports an invalid face or an absent service method. `SUCCESS` establishes one dispatch only. It does not establish progress, health, SETTLED, wire completion or permission to reclaim storage. The ordinary service context, serialization and lifetime rules still apply, with no hidden worker."

msgid "The optional [raw cycle probe](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/cycle_probe.h) brackets one selected vector or one explicit typed service call with real Arch counter snapshots. The initial generated path accepts `probe = true` inside `[uart.NAME.irq]` only for a reviewed F407/F470 IRQ-word UART selection. It adds one sidecar per physical vector and a pure typed getter for that sidecar. Unselected macros evaluate no arguments, create no sidecar and add no provider state or operations-table fields. The optional library is linked only when selected; linked ELF checks establish the actual default and selected cost."
msgstr "The optional [raw cycle probe](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/cycle_probe.h) brackets one selected vector or one explicit typed service call with real Arch counter snapshots. The initial generated path accepts `probe = true` inside `[uart.NAME.irq]` only for a reviewed F407/F470 IRQ-word UART selection. It adds one sidecar per physical vector and a pure typed getter for that sidecar. Unselected macros evaluate no arguments, create no sidecar and add no provider state or operations-table fields. The optional library is linked only when selected; linked ELF checks establish the actual default and selected cost."

msgid "The exact F407 Qiming USART1 and GD470 Liangshan USART0 word references now have linked probe-off/on evidence. OFF retains none of the optional observer's sidecar, probe/counter helpers, probe getter or observed-service symbols; ON brackets exactly one original provider IRQ dispatch. Their original provider state sizes remain unchanged. The links also retain the explicit service wrapper; they are not runtime I/O captures."
msgstr "The exact F407 Qiming USART1 and GD470 Liangshan USART0 word references now have linked probe-off/on evidence. OFF retains none of the optional observer's sidecar, probe/counter helpers, probe getter or observed-service symbols; ON brackets exactly one original provider IRQ dispatch. Their original provider state sizes remain unchanged. The links also retain the explicit service wrapper; they are not runtime I/O captures."

msgid "A readable counter pair is a raw modulo-2^32 difference, including probe cost and preemption. Multiple wraps, reset and clock-epoch continuity are unknown; `elapsed_known` is always false. The probe neither enables nor resets DWT. Unavailable samples and same-sidecar reentry are counted, and diagnostic totals saturate instead of wrapping. Different nested vectors require distinct sidecars. This is neither elapsed-time validation nor IRQ arrival latency, exclusive execution time or a passed budget."
msgstr "A readable counter pair is a raw modulo-2^32 difference, including probe cost and preemption. Multiple wraps, reset and clock-epoch continuity are unknown; `elapsed_known` is always false. The probe neither enables nor resets DWT. Unavailable samples and same-sidecar reentry are counted, and diagnostic totals saturate instead of wrapping. Different nested vectors require distinct sidecars. This is neither elapsed-time validation nor IRQ arrival latency, exclusive execution time or a passed budget."

msgid "Privileged Task snapshot saves and restores the incoming local interrupt mask for a bounded statistics copy. A task producer must use that same executor or be joined before reading; masking local IRQs does not join another preempted Task, core or security state. Reclaim joins all tokens, producers and readers. Typed UART-word and segmented-SPI service wrappers dispatch the original service once even when observation is unavailable. Observation failure never stops drain or releases a QUARANTINED borrow. Consumers must prove private state and borrowed storage disjoint from the optional observer. Raw probe samples cannot be promoted to validated timing budgets without independent continuity proof."
msgstr "Privileged Task snapshot saves and restores the incoming local interrupt mask for a bounded statistics copy. A task producer must use that same executor or be joined before reading; masking local IRQs does not join another preempted Task, core or security state. Reclaim joins all tokens, producers and readers. Typed UART-word and segmented-SPI service wrappers dispatch the original service once even when observation is unavailable. Observation failure never stops drain or releases a QUARANTINED borrow. Consumers must prove private state and borrowed storage disjoint from the optional observer. Raw probe samples cannot be promoted to validated timing budgets without independent continuity proof."

msgid "The [HIL measurement protocol](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/hil/README.md) uses schema 2 for measurement runs, contexts and traces. Cycle measurements require actual DWT endpoints, a live owner/epoch, admitted independent capture-clock facts and a CPU-frequency envelope covering that counter epoch and capture interval. This envelope must include actual oscillator tolerance, calibration and drift. A nominal rate or authored wrap limit cannot replace it. This does not change the separate SoC, OS or selected-mode raw protocols. IO-05 is implemented within this selected software scope; physical execution remains `not_executed`."
msgstr "The [HIL measurement protocol](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/hil/README.md) uses schema 2 for measurement runs, contexts and traces. Cycle measurements require actual DWT endpoints, a live owner/epoch, admitted independent capture-clock facts and a CPU-frequency envelope covering that counter epoch and capture interval. This envelope must include actual oscillator tolerance, calibration and drift. A nominal rate or authored wrap limit cannot replace it. This does not change the separate SoC, OS or selected-mode raw protocols. IO-05 is implemented within this selected software scope; physical execution remains `not_executed`."

