msgid "The dedicated [single-tuple LPTIM1 LPBAM reference](u575-lptim1-lpbam.md) adds one finite SRAM4 CCR1/RCR=0/ARR update under that same concrete Stop2 owner. The first word uses hardware request13 with BREQ1 and reserved DREQ0; two fixed continuation LLIs write RCR and ARR last. Explicit start/stop retains partial preparation and failed-drain responsibility. Fresh write-OK and all final-access proofs are necessary for success; success establishes synchronized register writes, not complete waveform playback. There is no GPIO route or physical HIL result, and general peripheral LPBAM and the original IO-32/SOC-35 exits remain open."
msgstr "The dedicated [single-tuple LPTIM1 LPBAM reference](u575-lptim1-lpbam.md) adds one finite SRAM4 CCR1/RCR=0/ARR update under that same concrete Stop2 owner. The first word uses hardware request13 with BREQ1 and reserved DREQ0; two fixed continuation LLIs write RCR and ARR last. Explicit start/stop retains partial preparation and failed-drain responsibility. Fresh write-OK and all final-access proofs are necessary for success; success establishes synchronized register writes, not complete waveform playback. There is no GPIO route or physical HIL result, and general peripheral LPBAM and the original IO-32/SOC-35 exits remain open."

